BUNDLED BENCHMARK DATA
----------------------

The evaluation suites in `suites/` contain samples redistributed from public
benchmark datasets. Both are MIT-licensed and therefore compatible with this
project's terms. Selection seeds, split names and per-file details are in
`suites/SOURCE.md`; each suite file's header records the exact benchmark, split,
n and seed used.

suites/reasoning.jsonl -- 500 items from the GSM8K test split.

    Cobbe, Kosaraju, Bavarian, Chen, Jun, Kaiser, Plappert, Tworek, Hilton,
    Nakano, Hesse & Schulman. "Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems."
    arXiv:2110.14168 (2021).

    Distributed by OpenAI at https://huggingface.co/datasets/openai/gsm8k under
    the MIT Licence. Note that the original repository
    github.com/openai/grade-school-math carries no LICENSE file; the dataset
    card in OpenAI's own Hugging Face namespace is the licence of record.

suites/knowledge.jsonl -- 500 items from the MMLU test split.

    Hendrycks, Burns, Basart, Zou, Mazeika, Song & Steinhardt. "Measuring
    Massive Multitask Language Understanding." arXiv:2009.03300 (2021).

    Distributed at https://huggingface.co/datasets/cais/mmlu under the MIT
    Licence. Copyright (c) 2020 Dan Hendrycks, per the LICENSE file at
    github.com/hendrycks/test.

suites/instruction.jsonl contains 20 prompts authored for this repository and is
covered by the MIT terms in `LICENSE`.


METHOD PROVENANCE
-----------------

No code from any third-party repository is included in this project.

The paired per-sample significance test implemented in `quantcheck/stats.py` is
an established procedure -- an exact one-sided McNemar / binomial sign test on
the discordant cells of a 2x2 agreement table. Its application to detecting
language-model degradations follows:

    Kuebler, Budhathoki, Kleindessner, Zhou, Yin, Khetan & Karypis. "When LLMs
    get significantly worse: A statistical approach to detect model
    degradations." ICLR 2026. arXiv:2602.10144.

That paper's reference implementation, github.com/amazon-science/LLM-Accuracy-Stats,
is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0, which would be incompatible with the MIT terms in
`LICENSE`. It was not used. The method here was implemented from the paper's
description, and the module's docstring states this.

Full citations, each carrying a resolvable DOI, arXiv ID or ISBN, are in the
"Related work & citations" section of `README.md`.
